sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant A as Sender GUI / Skill
  participant AC as Sender Local Core
  participant S as Colab Server
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  participant BC as Recipient Local Core
  participant B as Recipient GUI
  A->>AC: POST message with client_nonce
  AC->>S: authenticated HTTP command
  S->>DB: verify channel_members and commit message + seq
  DB-->>S: committed durable message
  S-->>AC: created message
  S-->>BC: WebSocket invalidation(channel_id, latest_seq)
  BC->>S: GET messages?after=last_seq
  S->>DB: verify membership and read ordered gap
  DB-->>S: durable rows
  S-->>BC: missing messages
  BC-->>B: reconciled view
  Note over BC,B: If WebSocket drops, GUI reconnects with bounded backoff.
  Note over BC,B: Cursor pull after reconnect repairs every missed frame.
